WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:11.219
[man 1] <i>I never thought</i>
<i>that my life would turn out like this.</i>

2
00:00:11.886 --> 00:00:13.888
[dramatic music playing]

3
00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:16.307
[man 1] <i>It's not like I expected much.</i>

4
00:00:16.391 --> 00:00:19.060
<i>I didn't think I'd be president</i>
<i>or a pop star.</i>

5
00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:21.479
<i>But still. I had dreams.</i>
<i>hopes. and goals for myself.</i>

6
00:00:22.605 --> 00:00:24.774
<i>And not one of them</i>
<i>involved standing on a bridge</i>.

7
00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:28.194
<i>staring down at the Han River.</i>
<i>ready to jump in.</i>

8
00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:30.488
[somber music playing]

9
00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:32.615
[man 2] Hey. Bae Jin-su. open up!

10
00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:35.326
[inaudible]

11
00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.120
"MR. BAE JIN-SU!"

12
00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.705
[ominous music playing]

13
00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:41.541
"COME ON OUT
AND PAY UP WHAT YOU OWE!"

14
00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.669
-[woman] Hi. Excuse me? It's just…
-[man 2] Yeah?

15
00:00:44.753 --> 00:00:47.881
-[woman] My baby's trying to sleep.
-[man 2] Oh. jeez. I'm sorry. lady.

16
00:00:47.964 --> 00:00:50.467
You see. a dirty rat lives here
who owes us 900 million won.

17
00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.510
-[woman] Oh… Let's go inside now.
-[man 2] Hey!

18
00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:54.429
-You said you'd pay us back!
-[woman] It's okay.

19
00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:56.473
-[man 2] One loan and you'd be rich.
-[horn blares]

20
00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.058
-[man 2] The hell?
-[gasps]

21
00:00:58.141 --> 00:00:59.559
[car horn blaring]

22
00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:00.560
[man 2] Huh?

23
00:01:00.643 --> 00:01:02.854
-Shit. there he goes! Damn it!
-[comical music playing]

24
00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:04.731
[man 2] Bae Jin-su. get back here!

25
00:01:04.814 --> 00:01:05.815
Come back. you bastard!

26
00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:10.070
[panting] Oh shit.

27
00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.032
[timpani booming]

28
00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:19.245
[orchestra tuning]

29
00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:23.833
[man 3] Hey. guys.
Sorry. we're shooting a scene.

30
00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.503
We've got this whole street blocked off.
so please. go around.

31
00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.754
[man 2 sighs]

32
00:01:29.714 --> 00:01:30.715
[man 3] That way.

33
00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.094
-Thank you.
-[man 2] Shit. Where did that fucker go?

34
00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:37.597
[Jin-su] <i>I'm sick and tired</i>
<i>of these loan sharks.</i>

35
00:01:38.389 --> 00:01:40.433
<i>I didn't want to borrow</i>
<i>from them in the first place.</i>

36
00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:42.852
-[woman 1] Sorry. but who are you?
-[man 1] That should work.

37
00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:45.021
-[Jin-su] What?
-[man 2] Not with that setup.

38
00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:47.357
[Jin-su] Hey.
I'm just passin' through here.

39
00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:50.276
-[woman 2] Last looks in five.
-[Jin-su] Excuse me.

40
00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:51.861
[man 1] Perfect.

41
00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:54.864
-[woman 2] Yeah. no. it's okay.
-[Jin-su] Oh! Celebs! [chuckles]

42
00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.533
-[woman 2] Just…
-[man 1] I can't do that.

43
00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:57.992
-[man 2] Hold on.
-[man 1] What?

44
00:01:58.076 --> 00:01:59.744
-[Jin-su chuckles]
-[woman 2] Are you ready?

45
00:01:59.828 --> 00:02:01.371
-Come on.
-[Jin-su] I have to ask.

46
00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.207
-Why are there always film shoots here?
-[woman 2] Oh. sure.

47
00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.543
-[woman 1] What?
-[Jin-su] Oh. nothing.

48
00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:08.378
-[chuckles]
-[woman 2] That looks good.

49
00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:11.756
[Jin-su] <i>You wanna show poverty?</i>
<i>Film on my street.</i>

50
00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.758
<i>All I wanted was to escape this place.</i>

51
00:02:13.842 --> 00:02:15.260
[suspenseful music playing]

52
00:02:15.343 --> 00:02:17.178
When will you leave this shithole?

53
00:02:17.762 --> 00:02:20.140
Our pal Won-seok
trusted me with his money.

54
00:02:20.223 --> 00:02:23.143
Guess how much he made. You wanna know?

55
00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:27.397
He got a loan for 500 mil.
and I turned that into three billion.

56
00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.440
He was able to retire after that.

57
00:02:30.775 --> 00:02:33.486
Look. you can save
all your measly paychecks.

58
00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:34.988
but where will that get you?

59
00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.115
You'll never buy a house at that rate.

60
00:02:37.699 --> 00:02:41.077
Our generation won't get rich
playing by the old rules.

61
00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:45.748
You wanna make bank. invest with me.
Don't you want a piece of the pie too?

62
00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.917
Your old pal can
make you a multi-billionaire.

63
00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.170
-Easy. Just stick with me.
-[grunts]

64
00:02:50.253 --> 00:02:51.713
[chuckles] Okay?

65
00:02:51.796 --> 00:02:53.006
[somber music playing]

66
00:02:53.089 --> 00:02:55.425
I guarantee it. man.
You still have a chance.

67
00:02:56.593 --> 00:02:59.179
[Jin-su] <i>That weasel told me</i>
<i>to gather all the cash I could.</i>

68
00:02:59.262 --> 00:03:02.473
<i>I got a bank loan.</i>
<i>then borrowed more from the sharks.</i>

69
00:03:06.477 --> 00:03:07.353
IN YOU. I TRUST

70
00:03:07.437 --> 00:03:09.355
-[line ringing]
-[Jin-su] Come on. pick up.

71
00:03:09.439 --> 00:03:11.357
-Damn it.
<i>-We're sorry. The caller is unavailable.</i>

72
00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:14.694
[Jin-su] <i>All day. news rattles on</i>
<i>about small businesses going under.</i>

73
00:03:14.777 --> 00:03:17.155
<i>That doesn't stop hundreds</i>
<i>of new shops from opening.</i>

74
00:03:17.238 --> 00:03:19.616
<i>Your chances of winning</i>
<i>the lottery are one in eight million.</i>

75
00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.951
I DON'T REALLY NEED A 600% PROFIT.
SO PLEASE ANSWER MY CALL

76
00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:24.162
<i>Yet thousands of lotto tickets</i>
<i>are sold every day.</i>

77
00:03:24.245 --> 00:03:26.206
HEY. YOU KNOW I EVEN BORROWED
FROM LOAN SHARKS

78
00:03:26.289 --> 00:03:28.041
<i>Only a few people profit</i>
<i>from trading stocks.</i>

79
00:03:28.124 --> 00:03:30.460
<i>But more and more keep trying.</i>
<i>Why. you ask?</i>

80
00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:31.377
PLEASE…

81
00:03:31.461 --> 00:03:32.712
{\an8}UNREAD

82
00:03:32.795 --> 00:03:34.380
<i>Because we're all deluded.</i>

83
00:03:34.464 --> 00:03:36.341
<i>We think losing's for other people.</i>

84
00:03:36.424 --> 00:03:38.384
<i>Not us. We'll succeed. we'll win.</i>

85
00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:40.970
<i>-You'll go bankrupt. I'll strike it rich.</i>
-Bae Jin-su. you idiot.

86
00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:42.055
[somber music playing]

87
00:03:42.138 --> 00:03:46.184
<i>We think we're the exception.</i>
<i>And that makes losing hurt more.</i>

88
00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:48.937
{\an8}"Can you find a word hidden in 'poverty'?"

89
00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.063
{\an8}"Over"?

90
00:03:52.607 --> 00:03:54.692
{\an8}"That's right. Game over."

91
00:03:54.776 --> 00:03:57.862
{\an8}<i>I worked ten years at my old job</i>
<i>and gave that bastard my severance.</i>

92
00:03:57.946 --> 00:03:59.072
{\an8}-[giggles]
-That fucking liar!

93
00:03:59.155 --> 00:04:01.449
{\an8}<i>He took my money</i>
<i>and ran without another word.</i>

94
00:04:01.532 --> 00:04:03.451
[jaunty music playing]

95
00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:06.412
<i>I got a part-time gig.</i>
<i>For under 10.000 won an hour.</i>

96
00:04:06.496 --> 00:04:07.830
TOTAL PAY 19.720 WON

97
00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:09.415
TOTAL PAY 29.580 WON

98
00:04:09.499 --> 00:04:10.833
TOTAL PAY 39.440 WON

99
00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:14.420
<i>At least I could save on groceries</i>
<i>by living off expired kimbap.</i>

100
00:04:14.504 --> 00:04:16.506
<i>I only made 78K a day.</i>

101
00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:17.715
TOTAL PAY 78.880 WON

102
00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:20.468
<i>No way I could pay off my debts</i>
<i>on that wage.</i>

103
00:04:20.551 --> 00:04:22.428
<i>I owed 900 million.</i>

104
00:04:22.512 --> 00:04:26.432
"SO I HAD NO CHOICE
BUT TO LOOK FOR A BETTER-PAYING JOB"

105
00:04:26.516 --> 00:04:28.726
[man 1] Anyone know
how to work with rebars?

106
00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:29.727
DAILY WAGE 160.000 WON

107
00:04:29.811 --> 00:04:30.687
WELDING

108
00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:31.813
[man 1] Any welders here?

109
00:04:31.896 --> 00:04:33.982
[Jin-su] <i>Ever since I was young.</i>
<i>my grandma would say…</i>

110
00:04:34.065 --> 00:04:35.066
DAILY WAGE 180.000 WON

111
00:04:35.149 --> 00:04:37.360
<i>"You need to learn a skill.</i>
<i>in order to make a living."</i>

112
00:04:38.236 --> 00:04:40.822
<i>Finally. I'm realizing</i>
<i>just how right she was.</i>

113
00:04:40.905 --> 00:04:42.782
[man 1] Here. this way for woodwork.
Thank you.

114
00:04:42.865 --> 00:04:45.702
-[Jin-su] <i>She should've stressed it more.</i>
-[man 1] Let's keep it moving.

115
00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:48.955
-[Jin-su] <i>Clearly. it didn't sink in.</i>
-[man] Who works with plaster?

116
00:04:49.038 --> 00:04:50.331
[man 2] <i>I do.</i>

117
00:04:50.415 --> 00:04:52.166
[Jin-su] <i>After four years at college.</i>

118
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:55.211
<i>I'm still just a useless.</i>
<i>good-for-nothing idiot.</i>

119
00:04:56.713 --> 00:04:59.716
<i>I needed something high-paying</i>
<i>that required no skill whatsoever.</i>

120
00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:01.134
[man 1] We need those numbers now!

121
00:05:01.217 --> 00:05:04.429
[Jin-su] <i>Finance guys trade stocks all day</i>
<i>and get paid millions--</i>

122
00:05:04.512 --> 00:05:06.597
<i>Scratch that.</i>
<i>Hundreds of millions per hour.</i>

123
00:05:06.681 --> 00:05:09.225
-[man 2] Look at our stock!
<i>-Look at 'em. sittin' in skyscrapers.</i>

124
00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:12.312
<i>Then there's me.</i>
<i>the one washing the windows. Hanging on.</i>

125
00:05:12.395 --> 00:05:14.105
-[man 3] Those stats.
-[man 4] Yeah. yeah.

126
00:05:14.188 --> 00:05:15.523
Put a sell on it. Short it.

127
00:05:15.606 --> 00:05:17.483
[wind whistling]

128
00:05:18.693 --> 00:05:20.153
[Jin-su] <i>High-rise window cleaning.</i>

129
00:05:20.236 --> 00:05:22.739
{\an8}<i>80.000 an hour.</i>
<i>Not a bad wage. right?</i>

130
00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:24.032
{\an8}<i>But it's also so dangerous</i>

131
00:05:24.115 --> 00:05:26.367
{\an8}<i>they had to pass a law</i>
<i>capping the work day at four hours.</i>

132
00:05:26.451 --> 00:05:27.744
{\an8}-[wind gusts]
-Oh. fuck!

133
00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:31.831
{\an8}<i>-That's a daily total of 320.000 won.</i>
-[yelps] Oh shit. man!

134
00:05:31.914 --> 00:05:35.251
{\an8}<i>Then again. four hours a day is</i>
<i>a long time to be hanging off a building.</i>

135
00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:36.210
{\an8}Oh. get me down.

136
00:05:36.294 --> 00:05:40.673
<i>Even if I somehow had the time</i>
<i>to clean every window in Seoul.</i>

137
00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:42.925
<i>it still wouldn't be enough</i>
<i>to pay back my loans.</i>

138
00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:44.010
<i>It's too late for me.</i>

139
00:05:44.093 --> 00:05:45.053
[car horns blaring]

140
00:05:45.136 --> 00:05:47.889
<i>I'll be paying off the interest</i>
<i>for the rest of my life.</i>

141
00:05:49.599 --> 00:05:53.853
<i>So. that's why</i>
<i>I decided this was my best choice.</i>

142
00:05:53.936 --> 00:05:55.146
<i>I chose to jump.</i>

143
00:05:56.606 --> 00:05:57.774
Let's do this. Bae Jin-su!

144
00:05:58.566 --> 00:05:59.734
[phone chimes]

145
00:06:02.987 --> 00:06:05.490
[shuddering]

146
00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:08.451
[whimpering]

147
00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:09.702
[muttering]

148
00:06:11.079 --> 00:06:13.581
1.000.000 WON DEPOSITED
HELLO

149
00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.000
[grunts]

150
00:06:17.752 --> 00:06:18.628
[chiming]

151
00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:19.962
1.000.000 WON DEPOSITED
I WANT TO

152
00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:21.089
1.000.000 WON DEPOSITED
BUY

153
00:06:21.172 --> 00:06:24.217
1.000.000 WON DEPOSITED
THE TIME THAT YOU HAVE GIVEN UP

154
00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.593
Huh? Hmm?

155
00:06:30.139 --> 00:06:31.015
One. two…

156
00:06:31.099 --> 00:06:33.976
<i>Someone's depositing</i>
<i>millions of won into my bank account?</i>

157
00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:38.064
<i>They want</i>
<i>to buy the time that I've given up?</i>

158
00:06:38.147 --> 00:06:40.149
[ominous music playing]

159
00:06:41.109 --> 00:06:43.945
Four million… And for what?

160
00:06:44.028 --> 00:06:45.738
1.000.000 WON DEPOSITED
IF INTERESTED

161
00:06:45.822 --> 00:06:47.865
1.000.000 WON DEPOSITED
PLEASE GET IN THE VEHICLE

162
00:06:47.949 --> 00:06:49.784
[car approaching]

163
00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:56.165
[tense music playing]

164
00:07:04.841 --> 00:07:08.219
[Jin-su thinks] <i>They want me… to get in?</i>

165
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:16.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

166
00:07:22.984 --> 00:07:25.153
Hey. uh… is this like. uh…

167
00:07:25.236 --> 00:07:28.698
uh. so… some kind of program
for preventing suicides?

168
00:07:29.991 --> 00:07:30.992
Uh…

169
00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:33.202
Are you…

170
00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.205
So. I guess Seoul is trying something new?

171
00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:37.665
This car's really cool.

172
00:07:37.748 --> 00:07:40.585
You know. I've seen some limos before.
but only from far away… [chuckles]

173
00:07:40.668 --> 00:07:42.753
This is amazing. Thank you.

174
00:07:49.552 --> 00:07:50.553
[hollow tapping]

175
00:08:12.867 --> 00:08:14.869
[projector whirring softly]

176
00:08:19.207 --> 00:08:20.625
[music fades]

177
00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:37.975
[Jin-su thinks] <i>What is this?</i>

178
00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:50.279
"Hello. and welcome to <i>The 8 Show."</i>

179
00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:54.575
"This show doesn't require any skills
or previously acquired knowledge."

180
00:08:55.159 --> 00:08:59.914
"All that we ask of you is
the time you were willing to throw away"?

181
00:08:59.997 --> 00:09:01.666
[projector whirring]

182
00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:08.089
"All necessary food and accommodations
will be provided to participants.

183
00:09:08.172 --> 00:09:11.384
and the available prize money
will accumulate as time passes."

184
00:09:11.467 --> 00:09:15.596
"When the allotted time is over.
the show will end itself automatically."

185
00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:18.558
"In the case that any participant
expires during the process.

186
00:09:18.641 --> 00:09:20.476
the show will immediately
come to an end then.

187
00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.645
regardless of how much time may remain."

188
00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:25.898
"Expire"?

189
00:09:27.775 --> 00:09:31.112
"Therefore. we ask that you pay
special attention to your safety."

190
00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:33.489
"If you do not wish to participate.

191
00:09:33.573 --> 00:09:36.409
please take the cab fare from
the table and exit the premises."

192
00:09:36.492 --> 00:09:39.370
[thinks] <i>There's 20 million won here.</i>
<i>This is insane.</i>

193
00:09:39.453 --> 00:09:41.831
"However. if you do wish
to continue with the show.

194
00:09:41.914 --> 00:09:43.499
please select one of the numbered cards."

195
00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:46.377
"You may then step into
and through the drapes."

196
00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:48.754
Maybe this is some sort of game?
[clears throat]

197
00:09:48.838 --> 00:09:50.840
[thinks] <i>So they provide room and board.</i>

198
00:09:50.923 --> 00:09:53.509
<i>And they'll pay me money</i>
<i>just to spend my time here.</i>

199
00:09:53.593 --> 00:09:55.511
<i>And killing isn't allowed.</i>

200
00:09:55.595 --> 00:09:57.513
<i>That means it won't be dangerous.</i>

201
00:09:57.597 --> 00:09:59.348
<i>This looks to me like easy money.</i>

202
00:09:59.432 --> 00:10:02.560
Hello? Is this just
all for some prank show?

203
00:10:04.604 --> 00:10:07.315
But they'd have me sign
somethin'. a waiver… right?

204
00:10:07.398 --> 00:10:10.568
[thinks] <i>Whoever's doing this already</i>
<i>deposited six million won in my account.</i>

205
00:10:10.651 --> 00:10:13.529
<i>And they're offering an extra 20 mil</i>
<i>just for showin' up.</i>

206
00:10:13.613 --> 00:10:16.824
<i>Plus. they hired a limo</i>
<i>and booked this theater.</i>

207
00:10:16.907 --> 00:10:18.826
What on earth's goin' on?

208
00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:25.958
[thinks] <i>Wait. that's strange.</i>

209
00:10:26.042 --> 00:10:28.836
<i>Why are some numbers missing? Bizarre.</i>

210
00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:31.756
<i>I just don't know what to do.</i>

211
00:10:31.839 --> 00:10:34.675
<i>Oh God. What if they're</i>
<i>organ harvesters or something?</i>

212
00:10:34.759 --> 00:10:38.471
<i>Okay. That settles it.</i>
<i>And 20 million won isn't nothin'.</i>

213
00:10:38.554 --> 00:10:40.973
Oh yeah. I've gotta run.
I'm such an airhead!

214
00:10:41.057 --> 00:10:43.934
I forgot about the… thing…
and I've gotta head out.

215
00:10:44.018 --> 00:10:45.436
It totally slipped my mind.

216
00:10:45.519 --> 00:10:47.563
I hope your show is a big hit.

217
00:10:47.647 --> 00:10:49.190
Okay. good luck with it!

218
00:10:49.815 --> 00:10:50.858
Thanks for havin' me.

219
00:10:51.984 --> 00:10:53.653
[phone chimes]

220
00:10:53.736 --> 00:10:55.071
[sighs]

221
00:10:56.656 --> 00:10:59.408
You're really makin' it hard
to turn you down. you know.

222
00:10:59.492 --> 00:11:01.035
but I really do have to get go…

223
00:11:01.118 --> 00:11:02.870
220.000 WON DEPOSITED
3FLOOR CONVENIENCE STORE

224
00:11:02.953 --> 00:11:05.122
CONVENIENCE STORE OWNER
SORRY. THINGS ARE HARD

225
00:11:05.206 --> 00:11:06.999
BUT HERE'S THE 220.000 WON FOR ONE WEEK

226
00:11:07.083 --> 00:11:10.211
YOU CAN REPORT ME TO THE LABOR OFFICE.
BUT WE'RE FRIENDS. RIGHT?

227
00:11:10.294 --> 00:11:12.129
Shit. But…

228
00:11:12.213 --> 00:11:15.257
[thinks] <i>A week's work</i>
<i>and I barely have anything to show for it.</i>

229
00:11:15.341 --> 00:11:16.842
<i>That's my reality.</i>

230
00:11:17.468 --> 00:11:21.347
<i>If I do walk out. nothing will change.</i>
<i>I'll still have my debt hanging over me.</i>

231
00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:22.765
PAY US BACK. BAE JIN-SU

232
00:11:22.848 --> 00:11:24.517
[projector whirring]

233
00:11:25.434 --> 00:11:28.938
<i>I was ready to jump off a damn bridge.</i>
<i>What could be worse than the life I know?</i>

234
00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:32.483
<i>All right. You can have my organs.</i>

235
00:11:32.566 --> 00:11:35.486
<i>I don't care. I'm not going back</i>
<i>to my minimum wage life.</i>

236
00:11:35.569 --> 00:11:37.363
<i>Fuck it. I'll do it.</i>

237
00:11:37.446 --> 00:11:40.282
<i>What's a game show compared</i>
<i>to hanging off a 40-floor building?</i>

238
00:11:41.367 --> 00:11:42.952
[tense music playing]

239
00:11:43.035 --> 00:11:45.121
[thinks] <i>Three is a solid number.</i>

240
00:11:47.998 --> 00:11:49.500
[Jin-su] <i>I was curious.</i>

241
00:11:49.583 --> 00:11:51.919
<i>If they could afford</i>
<i>to send me millions and a limo.</i>

242
00:11:52.002 --> 00:11:55.297
<i>even a stack just for showin' up.</i>
<i>they must have some budget.</i>

243
00:11:55.381 --> 00:11:58.134
<i>So. then… what would the prize be?</i>

244
00:12:00.428 --> 00:12:02.430
[music intensifying]

245
00:12:10.271 --> 00:12:12.565
["Mr. Lonely" by Bobby Vinton playing]

246
00:12:27.079 --> 00:12:30.082
<i>♪ Lonely ♪</i>

247
00:12:30.166 --> 00:12:33.753
<i>♪ I'm Mr. Lonely ♪</i>

248
00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:38.591
<i>♪ I have nobody ♪</i>

249
00:12:38.674 --> 00:12:43.220
♪ <i>For my own… ♪</i>

250
00:12:43.304 --> 00:12:44.972
-[music speeds up]
<i>-♪ I am so lonely ♪</i>

251
00:12:45.055 --> 00:12:46.807
<i>♪ I'm Mr. Lonely ♪</i>

252
00:12:46.891 --> 00:12:49.101
<i>♪ Wish I had someone</i>
<i>To call on the phone ♪</i>

253
00:12:49.185 --> 00:12:52.521
<i>-♪ I'm a soldier… ♪</i>
-[music distorts]

254
00:12:54.273 --> 00:12:55.858
[music speeds up]

255
00:12:58.861 --> 00:13:00.863
[sped-up music continues with static]

256
00:13:04.909 --> 00:13:05.993
[music fades]

257
00:13:06.076 --> 00:13:08.913
[static buzzes and fades]

258
00:13:10.998 --> 00:13:12.833
[Jin-su breathing shakily]

259
00:13:12.917 --> 00:13:14.919
[soft. ambient music playing]

260
00:13:21.717 --> 00:13:22.885
[Jin-su gasps]

261
00:13:22.968 --> 00:13:25.137
[tense. jazzy music playing]

262
00:13:42.738 --> 00:13:44.782
[Jin-su] Oh. this place is fuckin' huge.

263
00:13:46.826 --> 00:13:48.327
Only 24 hours?

264
00:13:49.578 --> 00:13:51.580
They made this place for one measly day--

265
00:13:51.664 --> 00:13:52.832
Uh--

266
00:13:53.999 --> 00:13:54.834
Hey.

267
00:13:55.876 --> 00:13:57.127
Hey. Hey!

268
00:13:58.504 --> 00:14:00.089
I'm locked in.

269
00:14:02.174 --> 00:14:04.176
[foreboding music playing]

270
00:14:18.107 --> 00:14:19.525
A staircase?

271
00:14:22.611 --> 00:14:24.864
I must be on the third floor.

272
00:14:43.173 --> 00:14:45.092
There aren't any elevators.

273
00:14:55.686 --> 00:14:57.479
[rattles handle]

274
00:15:01.317 --> 00:15:02.276
-[beeps]
-[door unlocks]

275
00:15:03.277 --> 00:15:05.321
Oh. Oh…

276
00:15:08.032 --> 00:15:10.159
I was right. I'm on the third floor.

277
00:15:13.287 --> 00:15:14.371
The hell?

278
00:15:14.455 --> 00:15:16.081
[crickets chirping]

279
00:15:18.876 --> 00:15:21.253
Man. I was expecting a nicer place.

280
00:15:35.851 --> 00:15:37.436
Is this real?

281
00:15:38.938 --> 00:15:40.439
Oh shit…

282
00:15:41.148 --> 00:15:42.900
It's just a screen.

283
00:15:44.485 --> 00:15:46.320
And these are all cameras.

284
00:15:48.155 --> 00:15:49.990
Why are there so many of 'em?

285
00:15:51.659 --> 00:15:54.745
-[machinery clangs and whirs]
-Jesus! What was that?

286
00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:16.350
"Please hand in
all your clothes. accessories.

287
00:16:16.433 --> 00:16:18.477
and all other personal items
you may possess."

288
00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:22.022
"Then we request that you please
change into the uniform we have provided."

289
00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:28.237
In front of all the cameras?

290
00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:29.905
[chimes]

291
00:16:35.494 --> 00:16:37.413
Ugh. I just bought 'em.

292
00:16:43.419 --> 00:16:46.797
"You can keep an eye on the accumulated
prize money by checking the scoreboard."

293
00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:48.632
-What scoreboard?
-[bell chimes]

294
00:16:48.716 --> 00:16:49.800
SCOREBOARD

295
00:16:51.301 --> 00:16:53.220
"Food and shelter
will be provided for free."

296
00:16:53.303 --> 00:16:56.015
"You can access the intercom
to buy anything else you may need."

297
00:16:56.098 --> 00:16:57.391
-[bell chimes]
-Intercom.

298
00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:00.060
"However. the price of any purchased items

299
00:17:00.144 --> 00:17:03.564
will be deducted from your individual
prize money at a special rate."

300
00:17:03.647 --> 00:17:05.524
[thinks] <i>What's the special rate?</i>

301
00:17:06.442 --> 00:17:09.987
"Items that you intend to use outside
your room can be purchased in the square."

302
00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:11.155
Where's that?

303
00:17:11.238 --> 00:17:12.448
{\an8}THE SQUARE

304
00:17:12.531 --> 00:17:13.741
Oh. I see.

305
00:17:16.201 --> 00:17:18.370
"All participants are required
to remain in their rooms

306
00:17:18.454 --> 00:17:20.456
from midnight until 8:00 a.m."

307
00:17:21.123 --> 00:17:23.751
"You are not allowed
to block the cameras."

308
00:17:23.834 --> 00:17:27.546
"Violating any rule will deduct
half of the individual's prize money."

309
00:17:27.629 --> 00:17:29.131
Half? That's crazy.

310
00:17:29.757 --> 00:17:31.508
Shit. shit. shit. shit!

311
00:17:31.592 --> 00:17:34.219
AND THE SHOW BEGINS AT MIDNIGHT

312
00:17:35.471 --> 00:17:37.806
-Uh…
-[thinks] <i>What? I only have a minute?</i>

313
00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:40.726
-Shit! Jesus. One minute?
-[urgent music playing]

314
00:17:40.809 --> 00:17:42.186
Okay…

315
00:17:42.269 --> 00:17:43.562
Oh shit…

316
00:17:45.689 --> 00:17:48.233
-[whirring]
-Huh? Shit! What… Hey…

317
00:17:48.734 --> 00:17:49.651
{\an8}THE SHOW BEGINS NOW

318
00:17:49.735 --> 00:17:50.611
What?

319
00:17:51.236 --> 00:17:52.237
[grunts]

320
00:17:53.989 --> 00:17:55.240
[gasps] Wait…

321
00:17:55.324 --> 00:17:57.159
Jeez. What the hell?

322
00:17:58.744 --> 00:18:00.120
Hey. one sec. No…

323
00:18:04.583 --> 00:18:06.460
-[beep]
-[whirring]

324
00:18:07.252 --> 00:18:08.962
[gasps]

325
00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:10.881
Ah shit…

326
00:18:10.964 --> 00:18:13.801
-The fuck? Jeez…
-[music fades]

327
00:18:13.884 --> 00:18:16.303
God. this place is full of surprises.

328
00:18:27.981 --> 00:18:29.650
-[quirky music playing]
-What the…

329
00:18:30.818 --> 00:18:33.987
The pockets are printed on?
Who's behind this shit?

330
00:18:35.364 --> 00:18:36.698
[bleep]

331
00:18:40.911 --> 00:18:42.246
What now?

332
00:18:42.871 --> 00:18:44.164
That's money.

333
00:18:45.666 --> 00:18:47.668
[mysterious music playing]

334
00:18:51.797 --> 00:18:52.923
[bleep]

335
00:19:05.978 --> 00:19:07.062
It went up.

336
00:19:09.648 --> 00:19:10.566
[loud tick]

337
00:19:11.275 --> 00:19:12.317
[bleep]

338
00:19:13.694 --> 00:19:15.737
[mysterious music continues]

339
00:19:18.615 --> 00:19:19.700
[yelps]

340
00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:22.202
[laughs and shrieks]

341
00:19:22.286 --> 00:19:24.037
[thinks] <i>90K. I just made 90K!</i>

342
00:19:24.121 --> 00:19:27.040
<i>-</i>Yes!
<i>-That's 30.000 won a minute. Fuck. yeah!</i>

343
00:19:27.124 --> 00:19:28.208
Yes!

344
00:19:29.251 --> 00:19:32.212
[loud ticking]

345
00:19:32.296 --> 00:19:34.089
[upbeat jazz playing]

346
00:19:34.173 --> 00:19:35.924
1 HOUR LATER (56 MINUTES TO BE EXACT)

347
00:19:40.554 --> 00:19:43.599
{\an8}[thinks] <i>I can't believe</i>
<i>this is happening. So. let's see.</i>

348
00:19:43.682 --> 00:19:46.018
{\an8}<i>I've been here for just under an hour.</i>

349
00:19:46.101 --> 00:19:48.687
{\an8}<i>That means my hourly wage here is…</i>

350
00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:50.355
{\an8}<i>1.8 million won.</i>

351
00:19:50.439 --> 00:19:52.774
{\an8}<i>Okay. okay. I need to calm down.</i>
<i>Let me think here.</i>

352
00:19:52.858 --> 00:19:55.068
{\an8}<i>It said 24 hours</i>
<i>on the scoreboard outside.</i>

353
00:19:55.152 --> 00:19:57.779
{\an8}<i>How much do I make a day?</i>
<i>180 times 24…</i>

354
00:19:57.863 --> 00:20:00.032
{\an8}<i>Then tack on the zeroes… How much is that?</i>

355
00:20:00.115 --> 00:20:04.912
<i>One sec.</i>
<i>Uh. so. two times 18. four times. and…</i>

356
00:20:05.871 --> 00:20:08.957
<i>Hold up. That's over 40 million won.</i>

357
00:20:09.041 --> 00:20:12.336
<i>Fuck! You could make that much</i>
<i>in a year and live pretty damn well.</i>

358
00:20:12.419 --> 00:20:13.462
<i>Hell. yeah. Jin-su!</i>

359
00:20:13.545 --> 00:20:16.882
<i>Yeah! Comin' on this show's</i>
<i>the best decision you ever made.</i>

360
00:20:17.549 --> 00:20:18.884
[breathing shakily]

361
00:20:20.052 --> 00:20:22.054
What if I can only stay one day?

362
00:20:22.137 --> 00:20:24.640
Ugh. it doesn't give a timeline.

363
00:20:26.558 --> 00:20:29.770
If I can stay here for a couple of weeks.
I'll be able to pay off my debt.

364
00:20:29.853 --> 00:20:31.355
I've gotta take a leak.

365
00:20:32.147 --> 00:20:34.650
Oh. is the bathroom
out in the square? Shit.

366
00:20:36.777 --> 00:20:38.987
YOU MUST STAY IN YOUR ROOMS
FROM MIDNIGHT TO 8 A.M.

367
00:20:39.071 --> 00:20:41.281
BREAKING A RULE DEDUCTS
HALF OF THE PRIZE MONEY

368
00:20:41.865 --> 00:20:43.283
Is this worth it?

369
00:20:43.367 --> 00:20:44.952
Oh. hey. there. I just…

370
00:20:45.035 --> 00:20:46.995
I need to… I need to use the toilet?

371
00:20:47.079 --> 00:20:49.414
Could I just step outside
for. like. one second?

372
00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:53.502
Are you there? Hey… [sighs]

373
00:20:54.294 --> 00:20:57.297
Are they for real? I'm not allowed
to piss in a toilet? [scoffs]

374
00:20:58.966 --> 00:21:03.136
[panting] Hey. could you at least help me
turn on the heater in here? It's…

375
00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:05.764
Well. it's pretty cold in here.

376
00:21:06.932 --> 00:21:09.643
I-- Did I lose you?
Hey. are you still on the line?

377
00:21:09.726 --> 00:21:10.644
[sighs]

378
00:21:10.727 --> 00:21:12.854
"You can buy things you need."

379
00:21:12.938 --> 00:21:15.399
[Jin-su] <i>Of course.</i>
<i>I knew there had to be a catch.</i>

380
00:21:15.482 --> 00:21:18.402
<i>Who would give away millions of won</i>
<i>without some strings attached?</i>

381
00:21:18.485 --> 00:21:20.112
<i>They want me to spend my prize money.</i>

382
00:21:20.195 --> 00:21:21.405
<i>-Is that it?</i>
-[picks up phone]

383
00:21:21.488 --> 00:21:22.739
Hello. uh…

384
00:21:23.323 --> 00:21:26.618
Could I buy… a blanket
and a hand-warming pack?

385
00:21:27.536 --> 00:21:28.912
[click]

386
00:21:30.205 --> 00:21:33.083
Oh! No. no. hold on. That can't…
that can't be right. Wait. Don't…

387
00:21:33.166 --> 00:21:35.043
Uh… Cancel. Sorry. N. N!

388
00:21:35.127 --> 00:21:36.878
No. no. There. Sorry.

389
00:21:37.963 --> 00:21:41.591
You… Well. we must've had
a little misunderstanding. I guess.

390
00:21:41.675 --> 00:21:44.303
Yeah. I just want one hand warmer.
and one blanket.

391
00:21:44.386 --> 00:21:48.682
You charged me for a whole box. I think.
So. one hand warmer. one blanket.

392
00:21:48.765 --> 00:21:51.435
That's it. Thank you.
Now. how much will that be?

393
00:21:51.518 --> 00:21:52.644
[click]

394
00:21:52.728 --> 00:21:54.730
One mil-- Wait. That's insane.

395
00:21:55.772 --> 00:21:57.065
One point…

396
00:21:57.149 --> 00:21:59.151
What the… There must be some mistake.

397
00:21:59.234 --> 00:22:01.486
Uh… uh… Just give me a sec.

398
00:22:03.864 --> 00:22:06.950
BUT THE ITEM COST
WILL BE DEDUCTED AT A SPECIAL RATE

399
00:22:07.034 --> 00:22:08.660
"At a special rate…"

400
00:22:08.744 --> 00:22:11.288
Um. let me cancel the order.
Just cancel it. Let me think.

401
00:22:11.371 --> 00:22:12.581
I'll call you back.

402
00:22:13.582 --> 00:22:14.583
Huh.

403
00:22:14.666 --> 00:22:17.627
[thinks] <i>I finally understand</i>
<i>the rules of this show.</i>

404
00:22:18.295 --> 00:22:22.424
<i>I'm making 43 million won a day.</i>
<i>or 1.8 million an hour.</i>

405
00:22:22.507 --> 00:22:24.634
<i>Let's figure out the special rate.</i>

406
00:22:25.969 --> 00:22:29.306
How much is a newspaper?
Just a regular daily paper from a store?

407
00:22:29.389 --> 00:22:30.223
[click]

408
00:22:30.307 --> 00:22:33.810
[thinks] <i>I know that paper would've cost</i>
<i>1.000 won back at the convenience store.</i>

409
00:22:33.894 --> 00:22:36.229
<i>So that's the "special rate."</i>

410
00:22:36.313 --> 00:22:38.774
<i>Everything for sale is a hundred times</i>
<i>more expensive here.</i>

411
00:22:38.857 --> 00:22:40.525
<i>Evens out my new wage.</i>

412
00:22:40.609 --> 00:22:41.902
<i>I get it now.</i>

413
00:22:41.985 --> 00:22:44.863
<i>I understand the point of this show.</i>

414
00:22:44.946 --> 00:22:48.158
<i>Ha! Clever! They're testing me</i>
<i>to see just how far I can go</i>

415
00:22:48.241 --> 00:22:49.868
<i>while spending as little as possible.</i>

416
00:22:49.951 --> 00:22:53.330
Whoever's behind this. they've got
no fucking clue who they're up against.

417
00:22:54.373 --> 00:22:56.124
<i>Come on. They thought I'd go…</i>

418
00:22:56.208 --> 00:22:58.418
"Oh. I'm so cold! I'll give you anything!"

419
00:22:58.502 --> 00:23:02.172
[thinks] <i>Like some whiny brat!</i>
<i>Hah! Please. I'm a pro at being poor.</i>

420
00:23:05.217 --> 00:23:08.345
I'd like… a pound of discarded newspapers.

421
00:23:08.428 --> 00:23:11.932
And then a bunch of boxes too.
Used cardboard. okay?

422
00:23:13.683 --> 00:23:14.976
[click]

423
00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:18.063
Yep. that'll do. Yes. sir.

424
00:23:18.980 --> 00:23:21.817
120.000. four times three is 12…

425
00:23:21.900 --> 00:23:23.819
So that's four minutes of my time.

426
00:23:25.237 --> 00:23:26.363
Okay.

427
00:23:27.864 --> 00:23:29.616
[rustling]

428
00:23:32.619 --> 00:23:33.995
[sighs]

429
00:23:34.079 --> 00:23:35.789
Ah. this rocks.

430
00:23:37.249 --> 00:23:38.667
Ah. this is great.

431
00:23:39.626 --> 00:23:42.671
[thinks] <i>Buying this stuff was the cost</i>
<i>of doing business. That's okay.</i>

432
00:23:42.754 --> 00:23:45.382
<i>All right. I barely spent anything.</i>

433
00:23:45.465 --> 00:23:48.510
<i>I won't spend any more.</i>
<i>and tomorrow. I'll take home 43 million.</i>

434
00:23:48.593 --> 00:23:50.387
I'll be so rich…

435
00:23:53.515 --> 00:23:55.392
I'll be so rich…

436
00:23:56.184 --> 00:23:57.853
-[crickets chirping]
-[snoring]

437
00:24:01.898 --> 00:24:03.775
Hello? Hello!

438
00:24:05.277 --> 00:24:07.946
Please. help me.
Please. get me a plastic bottle right now.

439
00:24:08.029 --> 00:24:09.781
Mm-hmm! Bottle!

440
00:24:09.865 --> 00:24:10.699
Yes! Yes!

441
00:24:11.575 --> 00:24:12.534
Ah!

442
00:24:13.535 --> 00:24:14.619
[moans]

443
00:24:18.457 --> 00:24:20.208
-[wings flutter]
-[birdsong]

444
00:24:28.216 --> 00:24:31.303
Oh man. they made a fake sunrise?

445
00:24:32.137 --> 00:24:34.181
[groaning softly]

446
00:24:42.772 --> 00:24:44.941
-[ticking]
-[thinks] <i>"Time is very valuable."</i>

447
00:24:45.025 --> 00:24:46.485
<i>"Your time is money."</i>

448
00:24:47.152 --> 00:24:49.446
<i>-Boomers love saying that kinda crap.</i>
-[bleep]

449
00:24:49.529 --> 00:24:53.158
<i>What would the "time is money" crowd make</i>
<i>of this crazy thing I'm goin' through?</i>

450
00:24:53.241 --> 00:24:56.244
<i>Because in this world.</i>
<i>time really. truly. without a doubt.</i>

451
00:24:56.328 --> 00:24:58.455
<i>actually literally is money.</i>

452
00:24:58.538 --> 00:24:59.748
[woman 1] 'Scuse me!

453
00:25:00.707 --> 00:25:02.584
Is everyone in their rooms?

454
00:25:03.418 --> 00:25:06.713
Can everyone come out here
so we can introduce ourselves?

455
00:25:06.796 --> 00:25:08.298
[Jin-su thinks] <i>Someone's here.</i>

456
00:25:08.798 --> 00:25:10.592
[woman 1] Are we all accounted for?

457
00:25:10.675 --> 00:25:12.385
Don't be shy. people. come on out.

458
00:25:12.469 --> 00:25:13.887
Over here. over here!

459
00:25:13.970 --> 00:25:16.348
-[laughs]
-[Jin-su thinks] <i>Wow. Three other people.</i>

460
00:25:17.098 --> 00:25:18.808
Uh. sure.

461
00:25:18.892 --> 00:25:20.268
[suspenseful jazz playing]

462
00:25:30.195 --> 00:25:31.905
Hey. uh. how…

463
00:25:31.988 --> 00:25:34.032
Wait. how are you walking on the water?

464
00:25:34.115 --> 00:25:36.451
It's fake. This is all fake. You see?

465
00:25:36.535 --> 00:25:39.538
-Look up there. that's our "sunlight."
-[projector whirring]

466
00:25:41.122 --> 00:25:44.292
[5th Floor] Have you seen
the scoreboard yet? Come on. let's go see.

467
00:25:44.376 --> 00:25:46.795
[gasps] Look at the time.

468
00:25:46.878 --> 00:25:48.171
[Jin-su] They added more.

469
00:25:48.838 --> 00:25:51.258
It was only at 24 hours yesterday.

470
00:25:51.341 --> 00:25:52.634
-Uh…
-[banging]

471
00:25:59.975 --> 00:26:01.601
[banging continues]

472
00:26:02.686 --> 00:26:04.729
[5th Floor] Uh. hi. good morning.

473
00:26:07.065 --> 00:26:08.858
-Nice to meet you.
-[man groans]

474
00:26:11.111 --> 00:26:12.320
[Jin-su] How's it goin'?

475
00:26:13.154 --> 00:26:14.322
[6th Floor coughs]

476
00:26:15.156 --> 00:26:16.116
[4th Floor laughs]

477
00:26:20.662 --> 00:26:22.789
-[scoffs]
-Hey. what do you think?

478
00:26:22.872 --> 00:26:25.875
Will they keep adding hours
every day that we're in here?

479
00:26:25.959 --> 00:26:27.377
[Jin-su] Oh. good question.

480
00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:33.258
[woman groans] If they keep
tacking on more and more hours.

481
00:26:33.341 --> 00:26:36.386
well. we might just
find ourselves trapped in here forever.

482
00:26:42.392 --> 00:26:44.811
Uh… why are you dressed like…

483
00:26:45.395 --> 00:26:46.229
Uh…

484
00:26:47.772 --> 00:26:49.357
[man] I don't think that'll be the case.

485
00:26:49.441 --> 00:26:51.651
There's a limit to everything.
especially time.

486
00:26:51.735 --> 00:26:54.988
They haven't given us too many rules yet.
The time must mean something.

487
00:26:55.071 --> 00:26:57.699
I'm sure there are still
many rules we don't know.

488
00:26:57.782 --> 00:26:59.409
[8th Floor] Oh. really?

489
00:27:00.452 --> 00:27:02.370
Well. then. I guess I don't know.

490
00:27:02.454 --> 00:27:04.456
[suspenseful jazz continues]

491
00:27:05.749 --> 00:27:07.000
Hmm.

492
00:27:08.251 --> 00:27:10.503
[5th Floor] So. do you think
this is everyone now?

493
00:27:10.587 --> 00:27:12.547
One. two. three…

494
00:27:12.631 --> 00:27:15.342
Hold on.
There should be eight of us down here.

495
00:27:16.384 --> 00:27:17.677
[6th Floor] Hey. you.

496
00:27:22.390 --> 00:27:23.850
[5th Floor] Hey. new friend!

497
00:27:23.933 --> 00:27:26.353
What are you doing up there? Come down!

498
00:27:28.021 --> 00:27:31.149
I suppose she must be a bit
on the shy side. right? Don't you think?

499
00:27:31.232 --> 00:27:33.902
She could be shy. or just kinda rude…

500
00:27:36.571 --> 00:27:37.739
[laughs]

501
00:27:38.823 --> 00:27:41.618
[5th Floor] Okay. so.
I see you're on the second floor.

502
00:27:41.701 --> 00:27:43.953
And you are on the eighth.

503
00:27:44.579 --> 00:27:46.456
Um… third floor.

504
00:27:46.539 --> 00:27:48.541
-[Jin-su] Yeah.
-Sweetie. you're on the fourth floor.

505
00:27:48.625 --> 00:27:51.878
I'm fifth. He's sixth. he's seventh.

506
00:27:52.462 --> 00:27:54.839
So. who's on first? Does… someone…

507
00:27:54.923 --> 00:27:56.174
[man] Good morning!

508
00:27:59.719 --> 00:28:01.346
Looks like I'm the last one here.

509
00:28:02.055 --> 00:28:05.225
-Sorry. I tend to be on the slow side.
-[Jin-su] Hey.

510
00:28:05.934 --> 00:28:08.019
-[Jin-su] Do you need a hand?
-Oh. gosh. no. I'm good.

511
00:28:08.103 --> 00:28:09.479
I'm used to it. It's okay.

512
00:28:09.562 --> 00:28:11.856
Oh. I'm. uh.
I'm staying on the first floor.

513
00:28:11.940 --> 00:28:14.901
-My name is. uh…
-[2nd Floor] Why bother with names?

514
00:28:14.984 --> 00:28:16.861
We'll never see each other again.

515
00:28:17.570 --> 00:28:18.947
I'm 2nd Floor. 'kay?

516
00:28:19.030 --> 00:28:22.992
That works for me. It would be
impossible to remember everyone's names.

517
00:28:23.660 --> 00:28:28.373
Sorry. do any of you know where
I might happen to find a bathroom here?

518
00:28:28.456 --> 00:28:30.542
-[2nd Floor] There's no pisser.
-[Jin-su] Huh?

519
00:28:40.343 --> 00:28:41.261
[Jin-su grunts]

520
00:28:42.470 --> 00:28:44.973
-Hmm. It's plastic.
-[suspenseful music playing]

521
00:28:45.056 --> 00:28:46.349
[hollow taps]

522
00:28:48.143 --> 00:28:49.394
It's all plastic.

523
00:28:49.477 --> 00:28:50.687
Nothing here is real.

524
00:28:50.770 --> 00:28:52.063
Oh. that's odd.

525
00:28:53.690 --> 00:28:54.774
[chuckles]

526
00:28:58.486 --> 00:28:59.821
[giggling]

527
00:29:00.905 --> 00:29:02.282
-[Jin-su] Huh?
-[4th Floor] What…

528
00:29:02.365 --> 00:29:03.408
[6th Floor] Really?

529
00:29:04.617 --> 00:29:07.871
-[7th Floor] Wow…
-[Jin-su] What the…

530
00:29:07.954 --> 00:29:09.581
It really is fake.

531
00:29:09.664 --> 00:29:11.875
Imitations that look real.

532
00:29:15.920 --> 00:29:17.672
So does this mean
the bathrooms are fake too?

533
00:29:17.756 --> 00:29:19.257
[7th Floor] I'm afraid so.

534
00:29:19.340 --> 00:29:21.634
[Jin-su groans] That's a step too far.

535
00:29:21.718 --> 00:29:24.971
[7th Floor] It seems they
must have removed the existing plumbing.

536
00:29:26.306 --> 00:29:28.433
It looks somewhat functional but isn't.

537
00:29:29.642 --> 00:29:31.728
And the same goes for our uniforms.

538
00:29:32.771 --> 00:29:36.691
They look classy at first.
but there's no real substance.

539
00:29:37.233 --> 00:29:39.819
Yeah. they could've at least
given us real pockets. Man.

540
00:29:39.903 --> 00:29:41.821
It's so silly. They're just outlines.

541
00:29:41.905 --> 00:29:44.157
Oh. it's the worst.
I didn't know where to put my key.

542
00:29:44.240 --> 00:29:47.911
I had no pockets. so I thought maybe…

543
00:29:47.994 --> 00:29:50.663
sticking it in my boxers
was the best choice for now.

544
00:29:50.747 --> 00:29:51.956
Yeah. that works.

545
00:29:52.040 --> 00:29:54.709
But. uh. what do we do without toilets?

546
00:29:56.795 --> 00:30:01.341
Yesterday. you know.
I figured we'd just be here for a day.

547
00:30:01.424 --> 00:30:05.637
So I bought those waste bags
that campers and truckers use.

548
00:30:05.720 --> 00:30:07.847
-Ah…
-You just do your business and go.

549
00:30:08.556 --> 00:30:09.641
-[Jin-su] I see.
-What?

550
00:30:09.724 --> 00:30:12.310
-Yeah.
-Where do you put it when you're done?

551
00:30:12.393 --> 00:30:14.103
You leave it in your room?

552
00:30:14.187 --> 00:30:16.564
Well. we can't take anything
we buy in our rooms outside.

553
00:30:16.648 --> 00:30:17.982
so I guess so.

554
00:30:18.650 --> 00:30:22.403
So that means we'll just
be buying them each day.

555
00:30:22.487 --> 00:30:24.739
Plus. they all cost way more than normal.

556
00:30:24.823 --> 00:30:27.992
[7th Floor] Or we might not have
to follow that course of action.

557
00:30:28.076 --> 00:30:29.702
There is another way.

558
00:30:29.786 --> 00:30:32.330
"Items to be used outside the room
can be purchased in the square

559
00:30:32.413 --> 00:30:34.833
via the intercom in the common area."

560
00:30:34.916 --> 00:30:36.960
"A special rate will still apply."

561
00:30:38.920 --> 00:30:42.048
Rule book. second paragraph.
somewhere on the fourth page.

562
00:30:42.131 --> 00:30:45.343
Are you sure we should buy stuff together?

563
00:30:46.177 --> 00:30:49.305
What if it's even more expensive
in the square? What's the rate?

564
00:30:50.765 --> 00:30:51.891
I'm not sure.

565
00:30:52.892 --> 00:30:55.770
We know that the rate in our rooms
is multiplied by a hundred.

566
00:30:55.854 --> 00:30:59.274
which means the showrunners don't
want us to access too many resources.

567
00:31:00.108 --> 00:31:03.278
Anything we buy in our rooms
has to stay there. or we'll be penalized.

568
00:31:03.361 --> 00:31:05.196
And there's a big delivery chute here.

569
00:31:05.280 --> 00:31:09.576
Therefore. I'm going to assume
they want us to buy things together.

570
00:31:09.659 --> 00:31:12.579
Well. maybe we should buy something. then.

571
00:31:12.662 --> 00:31:15.164
-It'll be like a test.
-Do we have to?

572
00:31:15.248 --> 00:31:17.041
I… I'm kind of scared.

573
00:31:17.792 --> 00:31:19.836
There's no place to see
our scores down here.

574
00:31:19.919 --> 00:31:23.631
So. what if we pay a ton.
but we don't realize it?

575
00:31:23.715 --> 00:31:26.718
That's a good point.
How about we all take a vote on it?

576
00:31:26.801 --> 00:31:28.469
It's only fair. What do you think?

577
00:31:28.553 --> 00:31:30.555
Why waste time doing a damn vote?
Let's just try it.

578
00:31:32.098 --> 00:31:34.183
-[4th Floor] Oh…
-[sighs]

579
00:31:34.267 --> 00:31:35.768
Marlboro Reds. down to the square.

580
00:31:35.852 --> 00:31:37.186
-A lighter. too.
-What the hell?

581
00:31:37.270 --> 00:31:40.982
-The fuck you think you're doing. dude?
-What? We were gonna buy shit anyway.

582
00:31:49.991 --> 00:31:50.867
[Jin-su] Oh…

583
00:31:51.451 --> 00:31:53.494
-[clink]
-[1st Floor] Oh! Did you guys see that?

584
00:31:53.578 --> 00:31:55.371
The time just went down. Look up.

585
00:31:55.455 --> 00:31:57.123
As soon as we got the pack.

586
00:31:57.624 --> 00:32:00.126
the scoreboard blinked. and it changed.

587
00:32:00.209 --> 00:32:01.461
How much did it go down?

588
00:32:01.544 --> 00:32:05.340
It… was 30 minutes. now it's 28.

589
00:32:05.423 --> 00:32:07.800
That means in the square.
we purchase items with time itself.

590
00:32:07.884 --> 00:32:10.053
not money. like in our rooms.

591
00:32:10.136 --> 00:32:11.846
How much do a pack of Marlboros
and lighter--

592
00:32:11.930 --> 00:32:12.972
[Jin-su] Five thousand.

593
00:32:13.932 --> 00:32:17.977
Marlboro Reds are 4.500 won.
a lighter is 500 won. so 5.000.

594
00:32:18.061 --> 00:32:22.398
Yeah… 5.000 won equals two minutes.
A minute's worth 2.500.

595
00:32:22.482 --> 00:32:24.859
Does that mean it's a better
idea to buy things together?

596
00:32:25.443 --> 00:32:29.238
Since if we'd have bought that in
our rooms. we'd have paid half a million?

597
00:32:29.322 --> 00:32:31.324
-Right.
-You think this affected our money too?

598
00:32:32.450 --> 00:32:34.744
[4th Floor squeals]
The prize money's the same!

599
00:32:34.827 --> 00:32:37.080
-Hey. wait--
-All of my money's still up there!

600
00:32:37.163 --> 00:32:39.874
-[1st Floor] When did she go?
-[Jin-su] When did you run up the stairs?

601
00:32:39.958 --> 00:32:44.045
[4th Floor] I ran up when he bought stuff
without any sort of plan.

602
00:32:44.128 --> 00:32:46.589
So. I just wanted to make sure.

603
00:32:47.090 --> 00:32:49.258
It's fine. though.
I got scared for nothing.

604
00:32:49.342 --> 00:32:52.804
Then. using the shared chute.
we can buy everything we need.

605
00:32:53.972 --> 00:32:55.515
And when the time runs out?

606
00:32:59.018 --> 00:33:00.770
We have 35 hours on the clock.

607
00:33:00.853 --> 00:33:05.149
If we blow it all on shopping sprees.
it'll go too fast and the show'll be over.

608
00:33:05.942 --> 00:33:07.235
[7th Floor] Yeah. that's correct.

609
00:33:07.318 --> 00:33:10.863
We don't know when they'll give us
more time. or how it's gonna happen.

610
00:33:11.614 --> 00:33:14.701
But when I look around and see the size
of this place. and the prize money…

611
00:33:14.784 --> 00:33:16.494
all the money they poured here…

612
00:33:17.745 --> 00:33:21.124
{\an8}I doubt they built all this
just to kick us out after a day or two.

613
00:33:22.375 --> 00:33:25.461
[2nd Floor] Rich people hate spending
money. though. They're all fucking stingy.

614
00:33:25.545 --> 00:33:27.463
The longer they keep the show running.

615
00:33:28.339 --> 00:33:30.425
the bigger the prize pot will get.

616
00:33:30.508 --> 00:33:32.552
[Jin-su] That's true. but…

617
00:33:32.635 --> 00:33:35.263
the uber-rich can make a profit
in their sleep.

618
00:33:35.346 --> 00:33:36.597
Their money makes money for 'em.

619
00:33:36.681 --> 00:33:38.975
I mean. I've heard of oil tycoons
spending a fortune

620
00:33:39.058 --> 00:33:41.269
just to rake their names
into the desert sand.

621
00:33:41.352 --> 00:33:42.270
They're that rich.

622
00:33:42.353 --> 00:33:45.857
They shell out hundreds of billions
to visit space like it's nothing.

623
00:33:45.940 --> 00:33:49.569
The amount they're spending on this show
could be pocket change.

624
00:33:50.361 --> 00:33:52.822
Shit. My ass is too poor
to think that way.

625
00:33:52.905 --> 00:33:56.743
First off. I think we should sit down
as a group. and discuss what to buy.

626
00:33:57.326 --> 00:33:59.704
-Only the essentials. okay?
-[5th Floor] Okay.

627
00:33:59.787 --> 00:34:01.748
[Jin-su] <i>We decided</i>
<i>to figure out what to buy.</i>

628
00:34:01.831 --> 00:34:03.583
<i>That turned out</i>
<i>to be easier said than done.</i>

629
00:34:03.666 --> 00:34:07.628
So. my room's got this really dry air.
so maybe we can get some toner and lotion?

630
00:34:07.712 --> 00:34:09.297
[Jin-su] <i>A necessity to one person…</i>

631
00:34:09.380 --> 00:34:10.798
I never wear that crap. though.

632
00:34:10.882 --> 00:34:12.550
[Jin-su] <i>…just seems silly</i>
<i>to someone else.</i>

633
00:34:12.633 --> 00:34:15.720
We should all get some pillows.
since we all need them for sleeping.

634
00:34:15.803 --> 00:34:17.555
[Jin-su] <i>One person's core essential…</i>

635
00:34:17.638 --> 00:34:18.848
I already bought one.

636
00:34:19.432 --> 00:34:20.892
How could you sleep last night?

637
00:34:20.975 --> 00:34:24.312
We should add pens and paper to the list.
since we can all use those.

638
00:34:24.395 --> 00:34:26.355
Hmm? Why? None of us are in school.

639
00:34:26.439 --> 00:34:28.232
[Jin-su] <i>…is totally useless to another.</i>

640
00:34:28.316 --> 00:34:30.359
I need to get sanitary pads.

641
00:34:30.943 --> 00:34:32.904
[Jin-su] <i>We put our brains together</i>
<i>to hash it out.</i>

642
00:34:32.987 --> 00:34:35.948
<i>Eight Homo sapiens.</i>
<i>wielding our collective brainpower</i>

643
00:34:36.032 --> 00:34:38.367
<i>honed by millions of years of evolution.</i>

644
00:34:41.079 --> 00:34:44.332
<i>After much debate.</i>
<i>we bought eight plastic buckets.</i>

645
00:34:44.415 --> 00:34:46.626
<i>eight rolls of toilet paper.</i>
<i>four packs of pads.</i>

646
00:34:46.709 --> 00:34:48.711
<i>four garbage bags. two types each.</i>

647
00:34:48.795 --> 00:34:51.297
<i>and. of course. four packs of cigarettes.</i>

648
00:34:51.380 --> 00:34:52.840
<i>For the good of the smokers.</i>

649
00:34:52.924 --> 00:34:55.093
So then… these are our toilets?

650
00:34:55.176 --> 00:34:56.677
-Yeah.
-[Jin-su retches]

651
00:35:02.517 --> 00:35:03.601
-[Jin-su sighs]
-[farting]

652
00:35:03.684 --> 00:35:07.146
<i>Jeez. All that fuckin' talk</i>
<i>just to get a place to shit.</i>

653
00:35:15.238 --> 00:35:18.157
36 MINUTES LATER
(AFTER TENDING TO PERSONAL NEEDS)

654
00:35:18.241 --> 00:35:21.744
[4th Floor] You guys. when do you think
they'll give us some food?

655
00:35:21.828 --> 00:35:24.163
I'm starving to death over here. for real.

656
00:35:25.248 --> 00:35:27.208
[5th Floor sighs] Yeah. same here.

657
00:35:27.291 --> 00:35:29.877
I didn't even have dinner last night.
I'm so hungry.

658
00:35:29.961 --> 00:35:32.296
They told us they'd
provide food and drinks and stuff.

659
00:35:32.380 --> 00:35:34.006
What's taking so long?

660
00:35:34.090 --> 00:35:37.260
What? Why haven't you eaten anything?

661
00:35:38.136 --> 00:35:39.554
They brought me lots of food.

662
00:35:42.640 --> 00:35:44.267
Where was it?

663
00:35:44.350 --> 00:35:47.186
Hmm… The chute thing in my room.

664
00:35:47.270 --> 00:35:48.813
[bell chimes]

665
00:35:48.896 --> 00:35:50.773
It brought me a whole feast.

666
00:35:51.399 --> 00:35:53.860
There were all these meal kits.
and some waters.

667
00:35:53.943 --> 00:35:56.904
So you got multiple meals? Just how many?

668
00:35:57.655 --> 00:36:00.783
12 lunchboxes and 12 water bottles.

669
00:36:00.867 --> 00:36:03.411
Wait. 12 of each?
Did you eat 'em all? All 12 meal kits?

670
00:36:03.494 --> 00:36:05.288
Well. each meal
was a little bit different.

671
00:36:05.371 --> 00:36:08.416
so I just tried a bite of each one
and saved the rest.

672
00:36:08.499 --> 00:36:10.418
And used the water to wash up.

673
00:36:10.501 --> 00:36:12.837
-Huh?
-[sighs]

674
00:36:12.920 --> 00:36:15.548
Well. I felt grimy after such a long day.

675
00:36:15.631 --> 00:36:18.551
But there was just enough
in those bottles to wash up with.

676
00:36:19.218 --> 00:36:20.803
[4th Floor] What the hell?

677
00:36:21.470 --> 00:36:24.765
Hey. wait a sec. Hey.
They gave you 12 of everything.

678
00:36:24.849 --> 00:36:27.101
That clearly wasn't all meant
for one single person to use.

679
00:36:27.185 --> 00:36:28.936
How could you just keep
all that for yourself?

680
00:36:29.020 --> 00:36:30.354
Wouldn't you?

681
00:36:32.356 --> 00:36:34.483
[Jin-su sighs] Of course not. No.

682
00:36:34.567 --> 00:36:36.319
Come on. Use some common sense.

683
00:36:36.402 --> 00:36:39.155
If they gave me 12 of somethin'.
I'd know to share it with the others.

684
00:36:39.238 --> 00:36:40.448
Hmm…

685
00:36:41.240 --> 00:36:43.451
That does make sense. I see your point.

686
00:36:44.118 --> 00:36:45.620
[suspenseful music playing]

687
00:36:45.703 --> 00:36:47.246
[6th Floor laughing]

688
00:36:53.461 --> 00:36:55.963
Give her a break. 'kay?
Uh. she just made a mistake.

689
00:36:56.047 --> 00:36:58.841
It was all delivered to her room.
and it was our first day.

690
00:36:58.925 --> 00:37:01.344
She must've thought
we all got the same delivery.

691
00:37:01.427 --> 00:37:03.304
8th Floor.
if you share what you have left.

692
00:37:03.387 --> 00:37:05.640
that would be the nice thing to do. yeah?

693
00:37:05.723 --> 00:37:07.516
Hmm…

694
00:37:07.600 --> 00:37:09.602
"Hmm?" What are you saying?

695
00:37:10.186 --> 00:37:12.730
[thinks] <i>Why is she stalling?</i>
<i>She's making me anxious.</i>

696
00:37:12.813 --> 00:37:16.025
[2nd Floor] What's up? So. you're a hog?

697
00:37:16.108 --> 00:37:18.819
You wanna keep it all and stuff your face
while the rest of us starve?

698
00:37:19.612 --> 00:37:21.739
-Hmm?
-Yeah!

699
00:37:21.822 --> 00:37:24.283
What do you have to be so selfish for?
It's not very nice.

700
00:37:24.367 --> 00:37:26.619
Stop playing games with us. Princess.

701
00:37:27.203 --> 00:37:30.206
Oh. It's not like I'm gonna eat it all.
I don't want it.

702
00:37:34.001 --> 00:37:36.921
[thinks] <i>Oh. what now?</i>
<i>Why is she takin' that off?</i>

703
00:37:37.004 --> 00:37:39.465
I only eat one meal a day anyway.

704
00:37:41.592 --> 00:37:44.220
I'll keep one.
Help yourself to all the rest. okay?

705
00:37:44.303 --> 00:37:47.473
I don't care much for food.
But I was thinking about the rules…

706
00:37:47.974 --> 00:37:51.936
Don't we have to keep things in our rooms?
We can't bring room stuff out here.

707
00:37:52.019 --> 00:37:54.021
So. I'd share with you all if I could.

708
00:37:54.105 --> 00:37:55.314
-How. though?
-[clapping]

709
00:37:56.774 --> 00:37:58.943
-[6th Floor laughs]
-[5th Floor] All right. all right.

710
00:37:59.026 --> 00:38:01.654
-Get dressed now. That's enough of that.
-Hmm.

711
00:38:03.406 --> 00:38:05.825
[7th Floor] She very well
could've thought we all had food.

712
00:38:05.908 --> 00:38:09.161
And now we can share whatever's left.
so it's no big deal.

713
00:38:09.245 --> 00:38:11.789
Since we're not allowed
to leave our rooms with any items.

714
00:38:11.872 --> 00:38:14.417
and they seem to be giving
everything to the 8th floor.

715
00:38:14.500 --> 00:38:16.961
I think they want us to use
the chutes to distribute food.

716
00:38:17.044 --> 00:38:18.296
What do you mean?

717
00:38:19.255 --> 00:38:20.172
[7th Floor] Look.

718
00:38:23.259 --> 00:38:24.927
See how it's structured?

719
00:38:26.262 --> 00:38:28.597
The chutes in our rooms
must all feed into each other.

720
00:38:28.681 --> 00:38:31.225
[2nd Floor] Wait a sec.
There's only eight of us here.

721
00:38:32.977 --> 00:38:34.478
Why'd she get 12?

722
00:38:34.562 --> 00:38:38.190
[thinks] <i>She's right. I wonder</i>
<i>what that means. Why doesn't it match up?</i>

723
00:38:38.274 --> 00:38:39.483
[1st Floor] So. that means…

724
00:38:40.067 --> 00:38:43.904
if you each take two meals
and water bottles. then I'll get none.

725
00:38:45.448 --> 00:38:48.492
-Since I'm the first floor.
-Then how will we make sure it's fair?

726
00:38:49.493 --> 00:38:52.955
What would stop the top four floors
from each taking three meals.

727
00:38:53.039 --> 00:38:55.875
leaving the rest of us with nothing
down on the bottom floors?

728
00:38:57.585 --> 00:39:00.963
[Jin-su] <i>Floor 8 will send things</i>
<i>down to 7. who'll send to 6. then 5.</i>

729
00:39:01.047 --> 00:39:03.632
<i>to 4. to me. to 2.</i>
<i>and finally to the first floor.</i>

730
00:39:03.716 --> 00:39:07.053
<i>This system creates a hierarchy.</i>
<i>separating the top from the bottom.</i>

731
00:39:07.136 --> 00:39:09.597
<i>The lower the floor you're on.</i>
<i>the worse off you are.</i>

732
00:39:09.680 --> 00:39:11.140
[7th Floor] First. let's go and check

733
00:39:11.223 --> 00:39:13.392
if we can send things down
from room to room.

734
00:39:13.476 --> 00:39:15.978
We can figure out
how to split things up after that.

735
00:39:16.062 --> 00:39:18.439
8th Floor. if it's not too much trouble.

736
00:39:18.522 --> 00:39:21.108
could you go up and try to send
the rest of the food down the chute?

737
00:39:21.192 --> 00:39:22.860
I might as well.

738
00:39:22.943 --> 00:39:25.446
It's not like I have
anywhere else to throw it out.

739
00:39:28.282 --> 00:39:30.785
-[7th Floor] Hey. one more thing.
-[8th Floor] Hmm?

740
00:39:30.868 --> 00:39:31.952
Could we come?

741
00:39:32.870 --> 00:39:35.039
Do you mind if we all go up with you

742
00:39:35.122 --> 00:39:37.708
so we can all check out the chute
together. to see how it works?

743
00:39:39.210 --> 00:39:40.127
All of you?

744
00:39:40.211 --> 00:39:41.879
Since it's the first day.

745
00:39:41.962 --> 00:39:43.631
I'd like to learn the ropes.

746
00:39:44.590 --> 00:39:46.592
Just for future reference. you know?

747
00:39:46.675 --> 00:39:47.718
-Huh…
-[4th Floor] I agree.

748
00:39:47.802 --> 00:39:50.262
We wanna trust you. but you gotta admit.

749
00:39:50.346 --> 00:39:52.807
it would be
a lot to ask of us to take your word.

750
00:39:52.890 --> 00:39:54.767
Right?
This way. we can all see for ourselves

751
00:39:54.850 --> 00:39:56.352
how many meals and bottles there are.

752
00:39:57.686 --> 00:39:59.522
Uh. yeah. but I think. you know.

753
00:39:59.605 --> 00:40:02.191
that maybe we shouldn't
barge into her room.

754
00:40:02.274 --> 00:40:04.944
It's not like we're at our home.
in our apartments.

755
00:40:05.027 --> 00:40:08.155
We use those rooms
as our bathrooms too. and. you know…

756
00:40:08.239 --> 00:40:09.532
I've got nothing to hide.

757
00:40:10.491 --> 00:40:11.951
Let's all go look.

758
00:40:12.034 --> 00:40:14.036
[pensive music playing]

759
00:40:16.705 --> 00:40:17.790
Uh…

760
00:40:25.923 --> 00:40:28.676
[7th Floor] If you think about it.
they're a scary bunch. right?

761
00:40:28.759 --> 00:40:31.554
-[Jin-su] Who?
-[7th Floor] Whoever designed this place.

762
00:40:32.555 --> 00:40:34.682
We have a rule book of sorts. sure.

763
00:40:34.765 --> 00:40:37.601
but it doesn't explain the show.
nor what we're actually doing here.

764
00:40:37.685 --> 00:40:39.812
They omitted all the important details.

765
00:40:41.105 --> 00:40:44.483
It feels scarier not to have
any clue of what to expect here.

766
00:40:57.329 --> 00:40:59.373
-[Jin-su] Let me.
-[1st Floor] Don't worry about me.

767
00:40:59.457 --> 00:41:01.333
[Jin-su] I don't mind. It's a long way up.

768
00:41:02.084 --> 00:41:03.794
-[1st Floor] Thanks for this.
-[Jin-su] Sure.

769
00:41:05.421 --> 00:41:07.298
[4th Floor] 3rd Floor.
you're so thoughtful.

770
00:41:07.381 --> 00:41:09.133
[5th Floor and 4th Floor panting]

771
00:41:09.216 --> 00:41:10.801
[5th Floor] Oh. She's right.

772
00:41:10.885 --> 00:41:13.345
-This is really kind of you.
-[Jin-su] Yeah?

773
00:41:13.429 --> 00:41:16.599
And you were spot-on earlier
about the cigarette prices.

774
00:41:16.682 --> 00:41:18.601
-How did you know the exact cost?
-[Jin-su] Uh…

775
00:41:18.684 --> 00:41:20.603
I used to work at a convenience store.

776
00:41:20.686 --> 00:41:23.355
I still remember
the prices of most things we sold.

777
00:41:23.439 --> 00:41:26.317
-If you're ever curious. just ask. I can…
-[4th Floor] Oh.

778
00:41:26.400 --> 00:41:27.276
Okay.

779
00:41:28.944 --> 00:41:30.863
Oh my. let me help you out.

780
00:41:30.946 --> 00:41:32.531
-[Jin-su] Sure.
-[1st Floor] It's okay.

781
00:41:32.615 --> 00:41:34.033
[2nd Floor] What the hell?

782
00:41:35.409 --> 00:41:36.785
[sighs]

783
00:41:36.869 --> 00:41:39.163
[tense music playing]

784
00:41:39.246 --> 00:41:40.873
[Jin-su] What's up? What is it?

785
00:41:40.956 --> 00:41:43.334
[tense music builds]

786
00:41:45.377 --> 00:41:46.712
I don't believe it.

787
00:41:54.512 --> 00:41:56.639
[4th Floor] Why is your room so huge?

788
00:41:57.932 --> 00:42:00.935
8th Floor.
you even have a bathtub in here?

789
00:42:02.269 --> 00:42:03.771
You mean you don't?

790
00:42:05.397 --> 00:42:07.274
I bought the candles
this morning. Nice. huh?

791
00:42:08.567 --> 00:42:10.778
[Jin-su] <i>Not only was her room massive…</i>

792
00:42:13.864 --> 00:42:15.241
-[bleep]
-[Jin-su] No way…

793
00:42:15.324 --> 00:42:17.284
How much did that just increase?

794
00:42:17.868 --> 00:42:20.496
It went up by hundreds of thousands
all in one go.

795
00:42:20.996 --> 00:42:22.456
But how did it…

796
00:42:22.540 --> 00:42:24.291
How come? My God.

797
00:42:25.125 --> 00:42:26.710
I just get 50 grand.

798
00:42:27.670 --> 00:42:29.088
You make that much?

799
00:42:29.171 --> 00:42:31.382
-That means…
-[4th Floor] Don't you?

800
00:42:32.841 --> 00:42:34.426
I only make ten thousand.

801
00:42:35.553 --> 00:42:36.387
A minute.

802
00:42:36.470 --> 00:42:40.474
[Jin-su thinks] <i>So that means each floor</i>
<i>pays a higher rate as you go up.</i>

803
00:42:40.558 --> 00:42:43.477
Uh. this is some fucked-up shit. God damn.

804
00:42:43.561 --> 00:42:45.729
Hmm? What?

805
00:42:45.813 --> 00:42:47.815
[Jin-su] <i>8th Floor was beyond compare.</i>

806
00:42:47.898 --> 00:42:50.109
<i>Her hourly rate</i>
<i>was worth more than any of ours.</i>

807
00:42:50.192 --> 00:42:52.736
<i>She was playing for half a billion a day.</i>

808
00:42:52.820 --> 00:42:54.321
-[giggles]
-Oh. shit…

809
00:42:55.197 --> 00:42:56.657
[dramatic music playing]

810
00:42:58.284 --> 00:43:00.286
[ticking]

811
00:43:04.540 --> 00:43:06.542
[dramatic music continues]

812
00:44:12.232 --> 00:44:14.234
[ominous music playing]

813
00:46:59.900 --> 00:47:01.819
[ticking]

814
00:47:30.138 --> 00:47:32.140
[comic music playing]

815
00:48:46.632 --> 00:48:48.634
[tense music playing]

816
00:48:49.305 --> 00:49:49.543
